course: dictionary
lesson: 15564
title: Surpass: better than before
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Surpass» is a formal word. It means to be better or greater than someone or something. «Jade ran faster than anyone in the school and surpassed the old record.» Here surpassed means beat, or did better than.
explain: It can also mean to go beyond what was expected or hoped. «The result surpassed our hopes.» Nobody thought the result would be that good, and it was even better. To check, swap in a plain word such as «went over»: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In maths, «the sales surpassed 500» means the sales became more than 500. You will meet surpass in reports, exams and grown-up writing, so it helps to know it well.
fact: Surpass means to be better than, or greater than, someone or something.
fact: Surpass is a formal word, so you will see it more in writing than in everyday talk.
fact: Surpass can also mean to go beyond what was expected or hoped.
fact: Plain words for surpass are beat, do better than, be more than and go over.
fact: The other forms of the word are surpasses, surpassed and surpassing.
exercise: «Jade ran faster than anyone and surpassed the old record.» What does surpassed mean? | Copied | Forgot | Hid from | *Beat
exercise: «The sales surpassed 500 this week.» What does surpassed mean here? | Were counted twice | Fell below 500 | *Became more than 500 | Stayed exactly at 500
exercise: Which plain word could replace surpass in «She will surpass her teacher one day»? | *be better than | copy | forget | sleep beside
test: «The result surpassed our hopes.» What does this tell you? | The result was hard to see | *The result was better than we hoped | The result was worse than we feared | The result was exactly what we planned
test: Which plain word is closest in meaning to surpass? | Hide | *Go over | Lower | Whisper
exam: «Our team surpassed its target, so we celebrated.» Why did they celebrate? | They missed their target | *They did better than their target | They forgot the target | They changed the target
